{"school":{"dbn":"09X117","name":"I.S. 117 Joseph H. Wade","boro":"Bronx","district":"09","district_label":"District 9","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":326,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"1865 MORRIS AVENUE, BRONX, NY 10453","phone":"718-842-6138","website":"https://www.josephhwade117.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/66143","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"The Wade Academies MS 117X begins the 2024 school year in \"Good Standing.\" We are a Community School that serves as a Beacon for our community. Through collaboration with our partner, The Community Association for Progressive Dominicans (ACDP) we have began transforming our learning community from the school in the neighborhood to the heart of the community. ACDP plays a pivotal role in the services we offer families. Weekly, Monday - Saturday, from 7 AM to 10 PM our building doors are open. Together, we provide students and families with support in: attendance, mentors, college trips, monthly family engagement activities, community service projects, mental health services and referrals, free vision screening and glasses, free dental services, on-site Immigration services, weekly parent classes, family health and wellness activities and workshops, monthly food pantry access, and for the previous two school years, access to a washer and dryer on-site with free detergent.   The Wade Academies MS 117X middle school is located in the Morrisania section of the Bronx. We have 359 students, where 35% of our student population are ELL\u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u0099s, 28% are Students with Disabilities, 95% have free and or reduced lunch, and 21% are STHP. Currently we share our learning community with The Young Women\u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u0099s Leadership 568X, an all-girls serving grades 6 \u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u0093 12 school.  We have a Traditional Bilingual Educational Program (TBE), Special Education Bilingual Program, and a freestanding English as a Second Language Program (FSESL) for our students in grades 6 \u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u0093 8.  We offer a continuum of services and programs for our Students with Disabilities.  We will continue developing rigorous standards-based Units of Study for all of our students inclusive of our Multilingual learns and Students with Disabilities; both of which are offered accelerated course work and opportunities to obtain HS Regents credits.    Our vision at Joseph H Wade Academies, guided by our core values of civic leadership, community, justice, and learning,  will foster an inclusive community that addresses the needs of all learners by cultivating a culturally, socially, and emotionally responsive dynamic learning environment that prepares all students to develop into curious, socially just, and high achieving citizens.   Our instructional focus is that, in all content areas, Wade Academy teachers will use data informed practices, embedded with RTI strategies, to design standards-aligned, robust grade level learning experiences that allow students to make their thinking visible through explanation and demonstration of their reasoning.  Teachers use data and artifacts of student reasoning to determine next steps for refined, responsive, and differentiated instruction in order to guide all students to grow and ultimately reach mastery in both literacy and mathematics. Our strategic partnerships allows us to provide our learning community with, differentiated and targeted professional learning opportunities for all of our teachers with on- site mentors, common and grade level planning times, as well as specific teacher teams to revise and implement curricula based on students qualitative and quantitative data and provide on-site coaching to teachers and teacher leaders.    As we reimagine our community for the 2024-2025 school year, we have established lab site classrooms in all content areas to support teacher development and practice.  Wade teachers begin the year with their quarterly instructional rounds cadence, determined by our Instructional Leadership Team.  This cadence will ensure that our teachers are engaging in personalized professional learning experiences aligned to our mission, vision, Next Generation Learning Standards, and the Danielson Framework for Teaching, that are embedded with culturally responsive practices.  We recognize that these systems and structures supports our collective goal to build capacity, attract and retain highly effective teachers, improve pedagogy, and increase student achievement.  To further support our student's diverse academic needs, the Wade Community will utilize both i-Ready and the All-In-One Platform to provide teachers with real time progress monitoring and personalized learning plans for each and every learner.  In order to increase our students self-agency and academic responsibilities, commencing in the 2024-205 school year, our teachers and students will engage in bi-weekly data chats and student led conversations, positioning our students as the drivers of their mastery.   Through are various partnerships with District 9, ACDP, Thrive Art, Girls on the Run, Anchor Health, Bronx Lebanon Mental Health Services, and Fordham University, to name a few, we will continue to build a robust menu of both enrichment and extending learning opportunities that have become imperative to the success of our learners. For the 2024-2025 School Year, we will be establishing a partnership that delivers mentorship to all of our young people,  providing on-site support to our students in the areas of self-identity, self-worth, and healthy lifestyle choices and Social Emotional Learning. In keeping with our theme to develop the whole child, we recognize that this is only possible through a partnership with our families. We have an open door policy for our families and make every effort to engage them through differentiated workshops, student performances, school activities and connections to outside family support services","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":"4 to 176th St; B, D to 174-175th Sts","bus":"Bx1, Bx18A, Bx18B, Bx2, Bx3, Bx32, Bx36, Bx40, Bx41, Bx41-SBS, Bx42, BxM4","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Tremont","latitude":40.8488,"longitude":-73.9089,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.986],"n":[152.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.914,0.909,0.967,0.876,0.871,0.881,0.9],"n":[530.0,492.0,426.0,441.0,405.0,399.0,378.0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null,1.0,0.881]},"attendance_remote_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.965],"n":[423.0]},"chronic_absent_ems_all":{"y":["2015-16","2016-17","2017-18","2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.694,0.747,0.684,0.731,0.67,0.928,0.51,0.533,0.558,0.619],"n":[602.0,629.0,554.0,520.0,461.0,419.0,420.0,392.0,391.0,365.0],"c":[0.726,0.732,0.726,0.718,null,null,null,0.598,0.79,0.634],"s":[3.4,3.13,2.11,2.94,null,null,null,2.46,1.8,1.05],"b":["above","above","below","below",null,null,null,"below","low","low"]},"chronic_absent_ems_allea":{"y":["2019-20","2021-22","2022-23","2024-25"],"v":[null,null,null,null],"st":["suppressed","suppressed","suppressed","suppressed"],"n":[2.0,1.0,1.0,1.0]},"chronic_absent_ems_alleb":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.67,0.651,0.9,0.597,0.551,0.563,0.632],"n":[94.0,83.0,90.0,72.0,69.0,64.0,76.0],"c":[0.674,null,null,null,null,null,null]},"chronic_absent_ems_alleh":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.745,0.675,0.935,0.495,0.528,0.554,0.619],"n":[411.0,363.0,321.0,325.0,318.0,314.0,278.0],"c":[0.727,null,null,null,null,null,null]},"chronic_absent_ems